				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${\chi }_{2K}^{2}=-2{\sum}_{i=1:K}{\log }_{{p}_{i}}$$\end{document}χ2K2=−2∑i=1:Klogpiwhere \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${p}_{i}$$\end{document}pi is the ith p-value, and χ2 has a chi-squared distribution with 2K degrees of freedom, then an integrated p-value can be determined. Similarly, Benjamini–Hochberg adjusted p-values are calculated.
